{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/CP_RTE","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/CP_RTE@rel:R20-11#c0cdcad9","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/CP_RTE","release":"R20-11","content":"Runtime Environment (RTE) The RTE realizes the Virtual Functional Bus (VFB) interface between Software Components (SW-Cs) and connects application components with the Basic Software (BSW). function Rte_Read / Rte_Write [SWS_CP_RTE_00001] Std_ReturnType Rte_Read_&lt;p&gt;_&lt;o&gt;(&lt;data_type&gt;* data); Std_ReturnType Rte_Write_&lt;p&gt;_&lt;o&gt;(&lt;data_type&gt; data); Explicit Sender-Receiver communication API for reading and writing data elements via component ports with transmission status feedback. function Rte_Call [SWS_CP_RTE_00002] Std_ReturnType Rte_Call_&lt;p&gt;_&lt;o&gt;(&lt;in_args&gt;, &lt;out_args&gt;); Synchronous or asynchronous Client-Server invocation across SW-C boundaries or down into BSW service components. function Rte_Result [SWS_CP_RTE_00003] Std_ReturnType Rte_Result_&lt;p&gt;_&lt;o&gt;(&lt;out_args&gt;); Retrieves the response and output arguments for asynchronous Client-Server calls once execution in the server has completed. function Rte_IRead / Rte_IWrite [SWS_CP_RTE_00004] &lt;data_type&gt; Rte_IRead_&lt;re&gt;_&lt;p&gt;_&lt;o&gt;(void); void Rte_IWrite_&lt;re&gt;_&lt;p&gt;_&lt;o&gt;(&lt;data_type&gt; data); Implicit Sender-Receiver communication API ensuring run-time data consistency within a Runnable Entity by snapshotting values at runnable entry and writing back at exit. function Rte_Enter / Rte_Exit [SWS_CP_RTE_00007] void Rte_Enter_&lt;area&gt;(void); void Rte_Exit_&lt;area&gt;(void); Enters and exits an Exclusive Area protecting shared resources from concurrent access by interrupting tasks or runnables.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"baseline_sync"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:43:28+00:00"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/CP_RTE","is_dropped":true,"first_active_release":"R20-11","last_active_release":"R20-11","dropped_